<title>USA: MVP buys Phoenix operations.</title>
<headline>MVP buys Phoenix operations.</headline>
<dateline>LA JOLLA, Calif. 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>MVP Holdings Inc said Friday it had completed the acquisition of the oil and gas operations and certain other assets of Phoenix Resources Technologies Inc in exchange for four million MVP shares.</p>
<p>The shares contain transfer restrictions and certain registration rights for a holding period of one year.</p>
<p>Phoenix reported that the historical cost for the oil and gas operations is $12.7 million.</p>
<p>The purchased operations consist principally of 125 miles of pipelines and oil and gas properties with 65 wells, and the operating rights to 12 wells in West Virginia and six gas wells in Louisiana.</p>
<p>MVP shares were trading at 3-1/2.</p>
</text>
